WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:01.767
-Welcome back.

00:00:01.767 --> 00:00:03.234
-Thank you so much
for having me.

00:00:03.234 --> 00:00:04.734
-Last time, I got to say, you
were on our show, I loved it.

00:00:04.734 --> 00:00:06.133
I also loved you brought
your dad.

00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:08.534
-Oh, my gosh. Yeah, my dad's,
like, obsessed with you.

00:00:08.534 --> 00:00:10.133
-Yeah, Leon is your dad.
-Yeah, definitely.

00:00:10.133 --> 00:00:12.400
He's always like, "You know,
I just -- I love Jimmy.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.334
He be having fun."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:14.334 --> 00:00:17.067
"Him and -- you know, him and
the Roots and they is all --

00:00:17.067 --> 00:00:19.133
they be having fun,
and Miley Cyrus comes on,

00:00:19.133 --> 00:00:20.601
and they do all them
little impressions."

00:00:20.601 --> 00:00:22.067
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.067 --> 00:00:25.367
He knows everything about, like,
Miley Cyrus and the impressions

00:00:25.367 --> 00:00:27.400
and the Roots because of you.
-Yeah, there you go.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:28.834
Well, thank you, Leon,
for watching. Hi, by the way.

00:00:28.834 --> 00:00:30.601
Hi, Dad.
-Yeah, hi, Dad.

00:00:30.601 --> 00:00:33.200
Hi, Papa.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.601
-Your parents are always
supportive of you.

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:37.601
But you told me that you got
really a lot of

00:00:37.601 --> 00:00:39.734
your comedy from Grandma.
-Yeah, totally.

00:00:39.734 --> 00:00:41.567
I think, like, there's two types
of grandmas.

00:00:41.567 --> 00:00:43.400
There's like
the milk and cookies,

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:45.100
"I'm going to knit you
a sweater" kind of grandma.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:47.100
And then there's, like,
the drinks, swears,

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:50.234
wants to go to Atlantic City,
have a Colt 45 kind of grandma.

00:00:50.234 --> 00:00:52.000
-Yeah, okay.
-And mine was the latter

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.100
and not the former at all.
-Really?

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:56.567
-Yeah, she liked, like --
She's no longer with us,

00:00:56.567 --> 00:00:58.267
but she really liked
"Late Night."

00:00:58.267 --> 00:01:00.167
Like, growing up, I would watch
"Saturday Night Live,"

00:01:00.167 --> 00:01:01.534
"Mad TV" with her.
She loved Conan.

00:01:01.534 --> 00:01:03.701
-With Grandma?
-Yeah, she loved like

00:01:03.701 --> 00:01:06.000
"The Critic," "South Park."

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.634
Like, she just -- she had
a really good sense of humor.

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:08.701
-"South Park"?

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.467
-She loved "South Park," yeah.
-Really?

00:01:10.467 --> 00:01:15.067
-Yeah, I remember she took me
to, like, opening night 'cause

00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:17.367
she was so excited about
the "South Park" movie.

00:01:17.367 --> 00:01:21.567
And I was really -- I was so
afraid of going because I knew

00:01:21.567 --> 00:01:23.334
she was watching me
for the weekend.

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:25.634
And I remember, like,
the opening number

00:01:25.634 --> 00:01:28.234
is just like a lot of
swear words.

00:01:28.234 --> 00:01:30.901
And I was like, "Grandma."
She was like, "Yeah?"

00:01:30.901 --> 00:01:32.734
And I was like, "I don't think
I can watch this.

00:01:32.734 --> 00:01:34.167
I'm going to get in trouble."

00:01:34.167 --> 00:01:35.834
And then she thought about it
for a second and she said,

00:01:35.834 --> 00:01:37.801
"Why don't you take your little
butt outside then?"

00:01:37.801 --> 00:01:39.868
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.868 --> 00:01:42.434
She was like, "I paid too much
for these tickets."

00:01:42.434 --> 00:01:44.834
-"I'm staying."
-Yeah, she said, "I'm staying."

00:01:44.834 --> 00:01:46.334
She told me to take my butt
outside.

00:01:46.334 --> 00:01:48.934
And, so then, I was like,
"Well, what am I going to do?"

00:01:48.934 --> 00:01:50.501
And so then, I just went to go
see, like,

00:01:50.501 --> 00:01:54.067
"House on Haunted Hill" alone,
which also traumatized me

00:01:54.067 --> 00:01:55.501
in, like, a very deep way.
-Yeah.

00:01:55.501 --> 00:01:56.767
Probably worse than "South Park"
would ever do.

00:01:56.767 --> 00:01:59.000
-Absolutely, yeah, totally.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:01.300
-There's so much great stuff
happening for you.

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:02.634
I just want to say
congratulations.

00:02:02.634 --> 00:02:04.501
It couldn't happen to a nicer,
more talented person.

00:02:04.501 --> 00:02:07.167
-Thank you.
-It just got announced yesterday

00:02:07.167 --> 00:02:09.868
that you're going to be in this
new series with Harrison Ford

00:02:09.868 --> 00:02:12.167
and Jason Segel called
"Shrinking"?

00:02:12.167 --> 00:02:14.834
-Yeah, I'm really excited, yeah.
-Pal, tell me about it.

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:16.634
How excited -- this is
Harrison Ford, I mean --

00:02:16.634 --> 00:02:18.300
-Yeah. I mean, it's unreal.

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:20.901
Like, I was already,
like, really interested

00:02:20.901 --> 00:02:23.601
because I'm a big fan of
Jason Segel and his work,

00:02:23.601 --> 00:02:25.234
and a lot of the people
that are working on it

00:02:25.234 --> 00:02:27.200
are, like, a lot of
the "Ted Lasso" people.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:28.701
-Oh, that's right,
it's the "Ted Lasso" crew, yeah.

00:02:28.701 --> 00:02:32.000
-Yeah, and it's over at Apple,
so I'm really excited about it.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.534
-But have you ever met
Harrison Ford?

00:02:33.534 --> 00:02:35.968
-No, of course not,
I haven't met Harrison Ford!

00:02:35.968 --> 00:02:39.534
If I -- Jimmy, if I met
Harrison Ford, you would know.

00:02:39.534 --> 00:02:41.901
I would rather, the next time
I see you, you introduce me

00:02:41.901 --> 00:02:44.167
and say, "Jessica Williams
from 'Shrinking,'

00:02:44.167 --> 00:02:46.634
has met Harrison Ford"
and then you bring me out.

00:02:46.634 --> 00:02:48.767
And then we go like this.
-And then we do this together.

00:02:48.767 --> 00:02:50.200
We make an offering,
yeah, of course.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:52.734
You never -- I'm sorry.
Well, you're gonna love him.

00:02:52.734 --> 00:02:54.234
-Oh, I'm excited.

00:02:54.234 --> 00:02:56.067
-He's funny.
-Good, I'm glad.

00:02:56.067 --> 00:02:57.968
-He's got a great sense of humor
and, yeah, you're gonna dig it.

00:02:57.968 --> 00:02:59.968
-Yeah, I start next week.
So I'm really excited about it.

00:02:59.968 --> 00:03:01.667
-Congratulations. I love that.
-Thank you so much.

00:03:01.667 --> 00:03:04.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you.

00:03:04.033 --> 00:03:06.033
-But let's talk
another great news.

00:03:06.033 --> 00:03:09.334
"Fantastic Beasts:
The Secrets of Dumbledore."

00:03:09.334 --> 00:03:10.601
This is giant.

00:03:10.601 --> 00:03:11.834
Eddie Redmayne was here
last night.

00:03:11.834 --> 00:03:13.033
-Did he do the manticore dance?

00:03:13.033 --> 00:03:14.801
-What? Yes, we did.
-He's obsessed.

00:03:14.801 --> 00:03:16.300
He's obsessed with
the manticore dance.

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:18.167
-Yeah, he showed me how to do
this really embarrassing dance.

00:03:18.167 --> 00:03:20.234
He looks cool doing it.
I looked like an --

00:03:20.234 --> 00:03:22.901
-You didn't look great?
-I looked like a comedian, yeah.

00:03:22.901 --> 00:03:24.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.534 --> 00:03:26.267
You joined the franchise
last movie.

00:03:26.267 --> 00:03:27.300
-Yes, just a little --

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:28.901
I made a brief appearance
in the last one.

00:03:28.901 --> 00:03:30.300
That was, like, years ago, so --

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:31.901
-Can you tell everyone
who you play?

00:03:31.901 --> 00:03:34.400
-Yeah, I play
Professor Eulalie Hicks,

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:36.267
who is the Charms professor

00:03:36.267 --> 00:03:37.868
at the North American
School of Ilvermorny,

00:03:37.868 --> 00:03:39.234
which we have not seen.

00:03:39.234 --> 00:03:41.501
And my character is brilliant.

00:03:41.501 --> 00:03:43.100
She's really warm and witty.

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:45.968
And essentially, Dumbledore
recruits her to help

00:03:45.968 --> 00:03:49.501
move against Grindelwald, who is
basically his bad ex-boyfriend

00:03:49.501 --> 00:03:51.834
that you're just like, "Ugh,
come on, guys, get it together."

00:03:51.834 --> 00:03:53.634
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.634 --> 00:03:55.634
We all have one.

00:03:55.634 --> 00:03:58.467
And so, anyway, all this,
you know, she's really good

00:03:58.467 --> 00:04:01.434
at defensive magic,
and she has these really cool

00:04:01.434 --> 00:04:03.968
defensive magic sequences that
I'm really proud of

00:04:03.968 --> 00:04:05.901
and that were, like,
the funnest to shoot, so --

00:04:05.901 --> 00:04:08.868
-You are a "Harry Potter" fan
way before this.

00:04:08.868 --> 00:04:11.033
-Yeah. Yeah, my teacher
started reading me

00:04:11.033 --> 00:04:12.868
the "Harry Potter" books
when I was in the third grade.

00:04:12.868 --> 00:04:14.901
-Me too.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.901 --> 00:04:17.701
Yeah, I'm the same age
as you are.

00:04:17.701 --> 00:04:19.434
-Absolutely.

00:04:19.434 --> 00:04:21.267
Absolutely, fellow millennial.

00:04:21.267 --> 00:04:23.334
-That's exactly right.
Yes, how cool.

00:04:23.334 --> 00:04:24.868
Let's get on our skateboards
after this and skate around.

00:04:24.868 --> 00:04:27.834
-Absolutely. And have
a hard time buying houses.

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:30.000
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.100
-But to go into this world,

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:34.801
do you kind of freak out
being on set?

00:04:34.801 --> 00:04:36.701
How much is real
and how much is CGI?

00:04:36.701 --> 00:04:38.267
-I mean, obviously,

00:04:38.267 --> 00:04:40.200
unfortunately the magic
is not real.

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:43.834
You know, but it felt like when
I was a kid and we would, like,

00:04:43.834 --> 00:04:45.701
play fight growing up,
and, you know, you play with

00:04:45.701 --> 00:04:49.234
an adult and you kind of do a
fake punch and then, you know,

00:04:49.234 --> 00:04:51.434
like, my dad would go, "Aaaah,"
you know?

00:04:51.434 --> 00:04:52.701
So we were doing that,

00:04:52.701 --> 00:04:54.367
but we had these incredible
stunt people.

00:04:54.367 --> 00:04:57.834
So I would kind of wave my wand
and things would happen.

00:04:57.834 --> 00:05:00.100
But it was just like a guy
laying on the floor, you know,

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:01.467
shutting the door.

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:03.100
So, a lot of that stuff was --

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:05.667
-Still. It's movie magic though.

00:05:05.667 --> 00:05:08.400
I do want to show a clip.
Here's Jessica Williams

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:11.000
in "Fantastic Beasts:
The Secrets of Dumbledore."

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:12.367
Take a look at this.

00:05:12.367 --> 00:05:13.968
-I'll tell you what.

00:05:13.968 --> 00:05:15.834
I'll give you the first shot.
-Go ahead.

00:05:15.834 --> 00:05:16.834
-Are you sure?

00:05:16.834 --> 00:05:19.000
[ Groans ] Oh, boy.

00:05:26.901 --> 00:05:29.734
-Last time I ever help
that woman out again.

00:05:29.734 --> 00:05:31.033
Lally?

00:05:31.033 --> 00:05:33.501
-Whoopsie, Frank, sometimes
I forget my own strength.

00:05:33.501 --> 00:05:35.901
I'll take it from here.
Thank you.

00:05:35.901 --> 00:05:38.033
-Welcome.
-Catch ya later, darling.

00:05:38.033 --> 00:05:39.300
-Bye, Stanley.

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:41.300
I'll be over for a game of
Befuddler Dudley soon.

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:43.100
-Alright.

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:44.601
-That's my cousin, Stanley.

00:05:44.601 --> 00:05:45.567
He's a wizard.

00:05:45.567 --> 00:05:48.300
-No.
-Please, it's early.

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:49.367
Don't make me work for it.

00:05:49.367 --> 00:05:50.667
-I said I wanted out
and I want out.

00:05:50.667 --> 00:05:51.934
-Come now, Mr. Kowalski.

00:05:51.934 --> 00:05:53.868
-Can't believe my therapist said
you wizards don't exist.

00:05:53.868 --> 00:05:56.667
[ Laughs ]
What a waste of money!

00:05:56.667 --> 00:05:58.601
-You do know I'm a witch, right?

00:05:58.601 --> 00:06:01.501
-That's exactly right.
Jessica Williams.

00:06:01.501 --> 00:06:04.534
"Fantastic Beasts:
The Secrets of Dumbledore"

00:06:04.534 --> 00:06:06.801
is in theaters and IMAX
April 15th.

